From f32db26ef86921b598d05bb1e89d21e3893618b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:25:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tests of the layouts per array and of the padding

Managers whose arrays have different layouts, or are padded, give the
results of a manager stored point by point to the bit, through the
integration, the end of the time step and the revert; the unused values
remain NaN; the views account for the padding; HDF5 files saved from a
padded manager are read by a manager which is not. The refusals are
tested: states of different paddings, unpadded arrays given by an
initializer, outputs given by an array to a manager whose layouts are
not uniform. The C, Fortran and Python tests cover one manager with
mixed layouts and one padded manager. The C test now returns the status
of its checks.
---
 bindings/c/tests/LayoutTest-c.c         |  69 +++++++-
 bindings/fortran/tests/LayoutTest-f.f90 |  43 +++++
 bindings/python/tests/LayoutTest.py     |  30 ++++
 tests/MaterialDataManagerLayoutTest.cxx | 206 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 344 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

